<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00013093> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00013093> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ,
                                                                                                "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7487-1936" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-11-19"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Cholesterol delivery to the plasma membrane by STARD5 and efflux by ABCA1 (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://holthuis-lab-uos.de" ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-11-19 edits by ccasalsc (ORCID 0000-0001-8769-177X), agreed with Vitalina, after review ~/review-6ab067da00013093-STARD5-ABCA1: (1) ABCA1 MF GO:0120020 -> GO:0034041 ABC-type sterol transporter activity (RHEA:39051, EXP PMID:35974019); (2) STARD5 occurs in cytosol: PMID:19474188 -> PMID:15897605 (human liver cytosolic fractions); (3) intracellular cholesterol transport part of response to ER stress: IDA PMID:31015253 (mouse hepatocyte KO) -> IMP PMID:40362395 (Fig. 4, Ad-CMV-hStarD5 rescue in StarD5-/- liver); (4) STARD5 part of intracellular cholesterol transport: IDA -> IMP PMID:31015253 (Fig. 4, human StarD5 overexpression)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "ABCA1 evidence PMID:11162594 and PMID:19556522 taken from existing experimental annotations; read as abstract only in this build. Built 2026-11-03 from review of gomodel:689e7a5d00005729."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Curated with GO AI HUB. STARD5 transfers ER-derived cholesterol to the plasma membrane, where ABCA1 exports it to apoA-I (cholesterol efflux); STARD5 acts in the ER-stress response."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Not modelled: ER-stress induction of STARD5 via XBP1 (PMID:23053693, mouse 3T3-L1 only; XBP-1(s) overexpression raises Stard5 mRNA, promoter reporter not responsive, mRNA stabilized; IRE1 not tested). NPC1 not modelled: no evidence of a causal link to STARD5."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "STARD5 input cholesterol deliberately left without a location: no paper measures the source compartment. ER is the authors' model (PMID:31015253), and PMID:23053693 proposes ER to Golgi; PMID:15897605 reports overexpression raising microsomal cholesterol."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "STARD5->ABCA1 link: shared plasma-membrane cholesterol node. Supporting data PMID:31015253 Fig. 1D: StarD5-/- mouse peritoneal macrophages show reduced ABCA1-dependent cholesterol efflux to apoA1; cyclosporine A abolishes the WT/KO difference; Ad-human StarD5 rescues efflux (mouse cells, human protein)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

